WEBVTT

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.238
because it's such a weird
thing to picture,

00:15:33.262 --> 00:15:35.226
this, like, virtual doorman

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:37.489
saying like, "Oh, hey,
like, here you are, too,

00:15:37.513 --> 00:15:39.856
calling into this conference call,"

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:42.446
but then also, it acts
as a great icebreaker.

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:45.466
AG: Alex, didn't just write
the hold music for UberConference.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:47.096
He cofounded the company,

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:49.408
and then went on to be
the lead product designer

00:15:49.432 --> 00:15:50.726
of Facebook Live.

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:53.990
So he's spent a lot of time
working on virtual communication

00:15:54.014 --> 00:15:55.454
and has a lot of experience

00:15:55.478 --> 00:15:58.059
building shared identity
and shared understanding.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:00.076
Alex's new start-up, Cocoon,